Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "RollingBallScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :EvidenceBasedAnomaly ;
    :hasEvidence :ball1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:ball1 a :RollingBallIndicator ;
    :indicatesPotentialRisk :risk1 .

:weather1 a :ClearCondition, :DayCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Rolling ball indicates potential child or pedestrian running into road" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: A ball rolling into the roadway serves as an evidence indicator for potential child-related collision risks, as children often follow rolling objects into traffic.
Severity Score: 0.75